            <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:27:47 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://arc.net/">https://arc.net/</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50197601">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div><section aria-labelledby="hero-title"><div><p>Arc is&nbsp;sunsetting on&nbsp;December&nbsp;22,&nbsp;2026.<br>Scroll to&nbsp;read what’s happening and&nbsp;see&nbsp;what’s&nbsp;next.</p><p><a href="#farewell">Read more</a></p></div><div><article id="farewell" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="farewell-title"><h2 id="farewell-title">We’ve decided to sunset Arc on December&nbsp;22,&nbsp;2026</h2><p>That’s not an&nbsp;easy sentence to&nbsp;write. We&nbsp;spent years building Arc and&nbsp;celebrating each and&nbsp;every release along the&nbsp;way: we&nbsp;have so much pride and&nbsp;love for&nbsp;what we&nbsp;made alongside the&nbsp;Arc&nbsp;community.</p><p>Our&nbsp;priority is&nbsp;to&nbsp;deliver best-in-class security for&nbsp;our&nbsp;members. Keeping a&nbsp;browser secure takes constant, dedicated&nbsp;work that is&nbsp;only increasing in&nbsp;the&nbsp;age of&nbsp;AI. Dia was built from the&nbsp;ground up to&nbsp;meet today’s security standards, so that’s where <span>our&nbsp;engineering and&nbsp;security</span> teams will focus moving&nbsp;forward.</p><p>We’ve worked to&nbsp;make switching to&nbsp;Dia as&nbsp;easy as&nbsp;possible for&nbsp;Arc members. Here’s&nbsp;how:</p><ul><li>Your passwords, bookmarks, extensions and&nbsp;history come over to&nbsp;Dia&nbsp;seamlessly.</li><li>Spaces, Folders, and&nbsp;Tab Groups are in&nbsp;Dia and&nbsp;import over with your data&nbsp;intact.</li><li>Dia now surpasses Arc benchmarks in&nbsp;stability, speed, and&nbsp;security.</li></ul><p>The&nbsp;browser features you use in&nbsp;Arc are&nbsp;free&nbsp;in&nbsp;Dia, and&nbsp;the&nbsp;AI is&nbsp;optional.</p><p>Thank you for&nbsp;using Arc, for&nbsp;pushing us to&nbsp;make it&nbsp;better, and&nbsp;for&nbsp;building alongside us. The&nbsp;team that made Arc is&nbsp;the&nbsp;same team behind Dia, and&nbsp;some of&nbsp;our&nbsp;most ambitious work is&nbsp;just ahead. We’d love for&nbsp;you to&nbsp;be there with us when&nbsp;it&nbsp;lands.</p></article></div></section><section aria-labelledby="timeline-title"><p><h2 id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2></p><ol><li><p>October 22</p><p>New Arc accounts can no longer be created. For&nbsp;existing Arc members, nothing will change yet. The&nbsp;latest version of&nbsp;Arc adds an&nbsp;option to&nbsp;export all of&nbsp;your data out of&nbsp;Arc, and&nbsp;an&nbsp;even smoother import&nbsp;into&nbsp;Dia.</p></li><li><p>November 23</p><p>On&nbsp;iOS and&nbsp;Android, Browse for&nbsp;Me and&nbsp;other AI features will be disabled. Arc&nbsp;Search will continue working as&nbsp;a&nbsp;browser, but you will no longer be able to&nbsp;sign in&nbsp;or&nbsp;sync&nbsp;your&nbsp;tabs.</p></li><li><p>December 22</p><p>You will no longer be able to&nbsp;access or&nbsp;use Arc on&nbsp;macOS or&nbsp;Windows. Arc accounts will be deactivated, with their personal data deleted within 30&nbsp;days. Arc&nbsp;Search for&nbsp;Android will be pulled from the&nbsp;Google Play&nbsp;Store.</p></li></ol></section><div id="move-to-dia" aria-labelledby="move-to-dia-title" data-greatest-hits=""><div><h2 id="move-to-dia-title">Moving to Dia is&nbsp;easy</h2><p>Import from Arc, and&nbsp;your setup comes&nbsp;with&nbsp;you.</p></div><div><article tabindex="0" data-feature="profiles" data-targets="[data-region=&quot;profile&quot;]" data-tag="Profiles"><p><h2>Your Spaces are now Profiles</h2></p><p>They come over to&nbsp;Dia with all your info. Use profiles for&nbsp;work, personal browsing, and&nbsp;everything in&nbsp;between. Swipe between them to&nbsp;switch contexts just like in&nbsp;Arc.</p></article><article tabindex="0" data-feature="sidebar" data-targets="[data-region=&quot;tabs&quot;]" data-tag="Sidebar tabs"><p><h2>Keep your tabs in the Sidebar</h2></p><p>Choose <em>Sidebar tabs</em> for&nbsp;the&nbsp;familiar vertical layout. Keep your tabs close by, or&nbsp;hide the&nbsp;sidebar with <kbd><kbd><img src="https://arc.net/farewell/assets/command-key.svg" width="11" height="11" alt="Command"></kbd><span>/</span><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><span>+</span><kbd>S</kbd></kbd> when you need to&nbsp;focus.</p></article><article tabindex="0" data-feature="pinned" data-targets="[data-region=&quot;favorites&quot;], [data-region=&quot;pinned&quot;]" data-tag="Pinned Tabs &amp; Favorites"><p><h2>Bring your Pinned Tabs and Favorites</h2></p><p>They come over from Arc when you import, with their custom names intact. Your everyday sites stay easy to&nbsp;reach.</p></article><article tabindex="0" data-feature="folders" data-targets="[data-region=&quot;folder&quot;][data-lead]" data-tag="Tab Groups"><p><h2>Folders come along, too</h2></p><p>They import seamlessly, now called Tab Groups in&nbsp;Dia.</p></article></div></div><section id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><p><h2 id="faq-title">Questions</h2></p><div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-1" inert=""><p>Arc for&nbsp;macOS and&nbsp;Windows will remain available until December&nbsp;22, 2026. Until then, Arc will continue to&nbsp;work as&nbsp;usual and&nbsp;will receive basic&nbsp;updates.</p><p>On&nbsp;December&nbsp;22, 2026, Arc for&nbsp;macOS and&nbsp;Windows will stop working, and&nbsp;you will no longer be able to&nbsp;sign in&nbsp;to&nbsp;your Arc&nbsp;account.</p><p>As&nbsp;of&nbsp;October&nbsp;22, 2026, new Arc accounts can no longer be created. Existing accounts are not affected by&nbsp;this&nbsp;change.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-2" inert=""><p><a href="https://www.diabrowser.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dia</a> is&nbsp;replacing Arc. It’s the&nbsp;new browser from the&nbsp;team that built Arc, and&nbsp;it&nbsp;keeps the&nbsp;Arc features you rely on, like vertical tabs in&nbsp;the&nbsp;Sidebar, Spaces (now called Profiles), Pinned Tabs, Folders, and&nbsp;Split View. You can bring your Arc data (passwords, extensions, profiles, tabs) over in&nbsp;a&nbsp;few clicks, and&nbsp;Dia is&nbsp;free to&nbsp;download for&nbsp;macOS and&nbsp;Windows at&nbsp;<a href="https://www.diabrowser.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">diabrowser.com</a>.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-3" inert=""><p>Yes, in&nbsp;just a&nbsp;few clicks during sign up. <a href="https://www.diabrowser.com/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download Dia</a>, and&nbsp;when it&nbsp;asks which browser to&nbsp;import from, select Arc. Dia brings over your passwords, history, tabs, Profiles, Folders, bookmarks, and&nbsp;extensions, on&nbsp;both macOS and&nbsp;Windows.</p><p>Already using Dia? You can import from Arc at&nbsp;any time before December&nbsp;22, 2026. On&nbsp;macOS, go to&nbsp;<strong>Dia&nbsp;&gt; Import from Another Browser</strong> from the&nbsp;Mac menu bar. On&nbsp;Windows, open the&nbsp;Dia app menu and&nbsp;select <strong>Import from another browser</strong>.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-4" inert=""><p>Yes. If&nbsp;you’re moving to&nbsp;Dia, you don’t need to&nbsp;export anything first, because Dia brings your logins, extensions, Spaces, Favorites, Pinned Tabs and&nbsp;Folders straight over from&nbsp;Arc.</p><p>If&nbsp;you’d like to&nbsp;use your tabs in&nbsp;another browser, you can save them as&nbsp;a&nbsp;list of&nbsp;links before December&nbsp;22, 2026.</p><h4>On macOS</h4><ol><li>Go to&nbsp;<strong>Arc&nbsp;&gt; Settings</strong> in&nbsp;the&nbsp;Mac menu&nbsp;bar.</li><li>Select <strong>Advanced</strong>, then <strong>Export Data</strong>.</li><li>Choose where to&nbsp;save the&nbsp;file, then select <strong>Save</strong>.</li></ol><h4>On Windows</h4><ol><li>Open Arc’s settings: press <kbd><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><span>+</span><kbd>,</kbd></kbd>, or&nbsp;open the&nbsp;Arc menu and&nbsp;select <strong>Settings</strong>.</li><li>In&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Advanced</strong> section, find <strong>Export Spaces and&nbsp;tabs</strong> and&nbsp;select <strong>Export Data</strong>.</li><li>Choose where to&nbsp;save the&nbsp;file, then select <strong>Save</strong>.</li></ol><p>Haven’t opened Arc in&nbsp;a&nbsp;while? You can still export your data before December&nbsp;22. Download Arc again using the&nbsp;link for&nbsp;your computer, then export your data from inside the&nbsp;app.</p><h4>On iOS (Arc&nbsp;Search)</h4><p>Tap the&nbsp;Tab Switcher icon in&nbsp;the&nbsp;bottom-left corner, tap Settings, then tap <strong>Export Data</strong> to&nbsp;share or&nbsp;copy a&nbsp;list of&nbsp;your open&nbsp;tabs.</p><h4>On Android (Arc&nbsp;Search)</h4><p>Tap the&nbsp;Tab Switcher (the&nbsp;stacked tabs button) in&nbsp;the&nbsp;bottom-left corner, tap Settings (⚙️), tap <strong>Storage</strong>, then tap <strong>Export data</strong> to&nbsp;share or&nbsp;copy a&nbsp;list of&nbsp;your open&nbsp;tabs.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-5" inert=""><p>We&nbsp;will deactivate all Arc accounts on&nbsp;December&nbsp;22, 2026. Once an&nbsp;Arc account is&nbsp;deactivated, personal data related to&nbsp;the&nbsp;account is&nbsp;deleted within&nbsp;30&nbsp;days.</p><p>If&nbsp;you have an&nbsp;account for&nbsp;both Dia and&nbsp;Arc, this will only affect personal data related to&nbsp;your Arc&nbsp;account.</p><p>As&nbsp;of&nbsp;December&nbsp;22, 2026, we&nbsp;will no longer be able to&nbsp;identify or&nbsp;retrieve Arc user data for&nbsp;data requests. To&nbsp;keep your data, export it&nbsp;from Arc or&nbsp;import it&nbsp;into Dia before December&nbsp;22, 2026. For&nbsp;instructions, see the&nbsp;FAQs “Can I&nbsp;export my tabs out of&nbsp;Arc?” and&nbsp;“Can I&nbsp;import Arc data into&nbsp;Dia?”.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-6" inert=""><p>Arc&nbsp;Search is&nbsp;changing on&nbsp;iOS and&nbsp;Android. Here’s what to&nbsp;expect on&nbsp;each&nbsp;platform.</p><h4>Arc&nbsp;Search on iOS</h4><ul><li><strong>October&nbsp;22, 2026:</strong> To&nbsp;save your open tabs, go to&nbsp;<strong>Settings&nbsp;&gt; Export Open&nbsp;Tabs…</strong></li><li><strong>November&nbsp;23, 2026:</strong> Browse for&nbsp;Me and&nbsp;other AI features turn off, and&nbsp;you can no longer sign in&nbsp;or&nbsp;sync with Arc. You’ll still be able to&nbsp;use a&nbsp;lite version of&nbsp;the&nbsp;mobile&nbsp;browser.</li></ul><h4>Arc&nbsp;Search on Android</h4><ul><li><strong>October&nbsp;22, 2026:</strong> To&nbsp;save your open tabs, go to&nbsp;<strong>App Settings&nbsp;&gt; Export Data</strong>.</li><li><strong>November&nbsp;23, 2026:</strong> Browse for&nbsp;Me and&nbsp;other AI features turn off, and&nbsp;you can no longer sign in&nbsp;or&nbsp;sync with&nbsp;Arc.</li><li><strong>December&nbsp;22, 2026:</strong> Arc&nbsp;Search for&nbsp;Android is&nbsp;deprecated fully, removed from the&nbsp;Google Play Store and&nbsp;from the&nbsp;devices it’s installed&nbsp;on.</li></ul></div></div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-7" inert=""><p>Until December&nbsp;22, 2026, you can reach our&nbsp;team through the&nbsp;chat on&nbsp;the&nbsp;Arc Help Center at&nbsp;<a href="https://resources.arc.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">resources.arc.net</a>. The&nbsp;Help Center also covers the&nbsp;full Arc deprecation timeline, how to&nbsp;move to&nbsp;Dia, and&nbsp;how to&nbsp;export or&nbsp;delete your Arc&nbsp;data.</p><p>Already using Dia? You can chat with Dia’s support team from inside Dia. On&nbsp;macOS, go to&nbsp;<strong>Help&nbsp;&gt; Chat with Support</strong>. On&nbsp;Windows, open the&nbsp;Dia app menu and&nbsp;select <strong>Help&nbsp;&gt; Chat with support</strong>.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div id="faq-answer-8" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-8" inert=""><p><a href="https://www.diabrowser.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dia</a> is&nbsp;made by&nbsp;the&nbsp;team that made Arc, and&nbsp;it’s where all of&nbsp;our&nbsp;focus is&nbsp;going, including our&nbsp;whole security team. It’s built from the&nbsp;ground up for&nbsp;today’s security threats, it&nbsp;has Arc’s greatest hits, and&nbsp;it’s a&nbsp;lot faster. The&nbsp;browser features you use in&nbsp;Arc are&nbsp;free&nbsp;in&nbsp;Dia, and&nbsp;the&nbsp;AI is&nbsp;optional. <a href="https://www.diabrowser.com/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Give Dia a&nbsp;try.</a></p></div></div></div></section></div></div>]]></description>
        </item>
